sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as Visitor
    participant B as Build page (Streamlit)
    participant M as RunManager
    participant H as RunHandle + Orchestrator (thread)
    participant L as events.jsonl
    participant VM as viewmodel
    participant C as components + graph

    Note over U,B: Step 1 - Describe
    U->>B: pick an example or type a request, press Build the pipeline
    B->>B: text_to_send (an unedited example goes out in its original wording)
    B->>M: start(request, files)
    M->>H: run() in a background thread
    B->>B: remember the run in the address bar (?run=...)

    Note over U,C: Step 2 - Build (the page redraws once a second)
    loop every second while the run is working
        H->>L: append events (agent calls, test results, stage status)
        B->>L: EventLog.read
        B->>VM: build_view(events)
        VM-->>B: RunView
        B->>C: run_dashboard(view, live)
        C->>VM: hero, journey_step, agent_states
        C-->>U: headline, live graph (lit stage and agent), Details closed
    end

    Note over U,C: Step 3 - Approve
    H->>L: approval_requested (rows are staged, nothing is loaded)
    B->>C: run_dashboard draws the approval gate, proofs and a preview
    alt the visitor approves
        U->>B: name, Approve and load
        B->>M: decide(run_id, approved, by, note)
        M->>H: decide - promote with a token bound to the staged rows
        H->>L: approval_decision, load_finished, run_finished
        C-->>U: gate open, database lit, first rows of the loaded table
    else the visitor rejects
        U->>B: Reject
        B->>M: decide(run_id, rejected, by, note)
        H->>L: approval_decision, run_finished (rejected)
        C-->>U: Rejected - nothing was written
    end

    Note over U,C: Past runs - replay uses the same code on a prefix of the log
    U->>B: open Past runs, press Replay
    loop every 0.6 s, n grows by the chosen speed
        B->>VM: build_view(events[0..n])
        B->>C: run_dashboard(view, replay)
    end
